he Silver Challenge Cup","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The Coupe des Mousquetaires honours the four ''Musketeers'' who won France the 1927 Davis Cup."},{"id":"q6","question":"Which venue, the largest tennis stadium in the world, hosts the US Open final?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Rod Laver Arena","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"Centre Court","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Arthur Ashe Stadium","is_correct":true},{"id":"d","text":"Court Philippe-Chatrier","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Arthur Ashe Stadium seats almost 24,000 people and opened in 1997."},{"id":"q7","question":"Wimbledon''s dress code famously requires players to wear what?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The club''s green and purple","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"Almost entirely white clothing","is_correct":true},{"id":"c","text":"Long trousers or skirts","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Clothing without sponsor logos","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The all-white rule at the All England Club dates back to the Victorian era."},{"id":"q8","question":"Which Grand Slam is nicknamed the ''Happy Slam''?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"US Open","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"Roland Garros","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Wimbledon","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Australian Open","is_correct":true}],"explanation":"Players call the Australian Open the Happy Slam for its relaxed January atmosphere."}]'::jsonb,
  null,
  array['tennis', 'grand slam', 'sports', 'trivia']::text[],
  3,
  'published',
